INT. ICE ARENA - ZAMBONI BAY - NIGHT

Concrete. Fluorescent hum. A resurfacer idles, steam rising off its blade. Puddles on the floor.

LUCIANA FERRARI-OYELE, 20s, goalie, pads strapped on, sits on an upturned bucket. Helmet on her knee.

DEACON BRUNO, 60s, driver, climbs down from the machine with a coffee. Slow knees.

LUCIANA
You're late, Deacon.

DEACON
You're early, Lu.

He sits on a second bucket. Offers the coffee. She shakes her head.

Silence. Compressor thrum.

LUCIANA
Three hundred shots.

DEACON
That a goal?

LUCIANA
That's tonight. Before they flood the ice.

DEACON
You'll wear a hole in the crease.

LUCIANA
Good.

A wall speaker CRACKLES.

BARTOSZ (V.O.)
(over PA, tinny)
Deacon, you in the bay?

DEACON
(not moving)
Where else.

BARTOSZ (V.O.)
Hold the flood. Coach wants Luciana out there another hour.

Deacon looks at Luciana. She looks at the floor.

DEACON
She's already here, Bart.

BARTOSZ (V.O.)
Then she's early. Tell her thanks.

Click. Silence.

LUCIANA
He doesn't know I'm out of the lineup.

DEACON
Tell him.

LUCIANA
Tomorrow.

DEACON
Tomorrow, Lu, I'll be flooding ice you're not on.

She pulls her helmet down. Stands. Bangs her stick twice on the concrete.

LUCIANA
Open the door, Deacon.

He climbs back on the machine. Lifts the gate. Cold light pours across the ice.
